Host Discovery with ARP
When our device is connected on the local network and perform -sn scanning using nmap for that local network, nmap will using 
ARP protocol as a priority option, in the case of the same local network, using ARP is more reliable than using ICMP.
Because ICMP echo packets could be blocked by the firewall, but it doesn't affect to ARP request. Our attack machine will send 
a ARP Broadcast Requests(Layer 2) to all devices that is available within a range of the network,
and waiting for ARP reply to identify target status.


